{
  "item": "MagicSkeleton01",
  "mu_name": "Magic Skeleton",
  "mu_name_from": "MuMain _enum.h MONSTER_MAGIC_SKELETON_1 (89), drawn as MODEL_MAGIC_SKELETON = MODEL_MONSTER01 + 62, so OpenMonsterModel loads Monster63.bmd; the client's name is 마법해골, 'magic skull' (ZzzCharacter.cpp:13405). WebZen's Monster.txt:117 calls breed 89 'Spirit Sorcerer', the castle's quota-2 breed; MuMain's English client and OpenMU S6 BloodCastle1.cs call it Magic Skeleton. docs/blood-castle-port.md Part B 3.",
  "world": "bloodcastle",
  "object_type": 89,
  "monster": {
    "model_index": 62,
    "scale": 1.2
  },
  "monster_from": "ZzzCharacter.cpp:13393-13406, CreateMonster, case MONSTER_MAGIC_SKELETON_1..8: OpenMonsterModel(MONSTER_MODEL_MAGIC_SKELETON); CreateCharacter(Key, MODEL_MAGIC_SKELETON, ...); Weapon[0] = MODEL_STAFF at Level 11; Scale = 1.2f. Its attack (MoveCharacterVisual's attack switch, ZzzCharacter.cpp:2071-2083): at attack time 14, from bone 33, MODEL_PIERCING+1 and a BITMAP_JOINT_THUNDER joint to the target -- a lightning bolt, so its attack_skill here is Lightning (3), the Devil's and the Thunder Lich's.",
  "right_hand": "Staff01",
  "right_hand_bone": "knife_gdf",
  "right_hand_from": "MODEL_STAFF is Item/Staff01.bmd, the Skull Staff (cooked). MODEL_MAGIC_SKELETON is not in CreateCharacter's weapon-link switch; bone 33, knife_gdf under the right hand, is where its lightning leaves from and where the knights' switch puts Weapon[0]. MU's Level 11 is not carried: a held weapon is +0 here.",
  "profile": "monster",
  "rig_from": "Seven actions, exported with --actions=all. 55 bones.",
  "sheets": {
    "bsh01": "magicskeleton_bsh01.png",
    "bons": "bons.png",
    "bsh02": "magicskeleton_bsh02.png",
    "bsh03": "magicskeleton_bsh03.png"
  },
  "sheet_from": "Four meshes: bsh01.OZJ (128x256, no alpha: the robe and the armour, 645 triangles), bons (the Skeleton's, shared: the skull, 56), bsh02.OZT (32x64, the red cloth strip, cut out, 47) and bsh03.OZT (32x32, a purple wisp of flame, cut out, 56). Decoded under a magicskeleton_ prefix.",
  "sheet_materials": {
    "bsh01": "cloth",
    "bons": "bone",
    "bsh02": "cloth",
    "bsh03": "cloth"
  },
  "sheet_materials_from": "Read off the sheets at 2x: bsh01 is a dark red robe with gold seams over black lacquered plate on the legs and arms; bsh02 the same red cloth, bsh03 a wisp. All cloth: the plate shares its island with the robe (island 7, 292 triangles), so it takes the robe's, its black kept as the sheet paints it. bons the skull, bone.",
  "cutout": [
    "bsh02",
    "bsh03"
  ],
  "cutout_from": "bsh02 and bsh03 are .OZT, their alpha cut.",
  "glow": {
    "bsh02": {
      "pulse": [
        0.0,
        1.0
      ]
    }
  },
  "glow_from": "ZzzObject.cpp:1250-1254, the render switch, MODEL_MAGIC_SKELETON: RenderBody as usual, then RenderMesh(2, RENDER_TEXTURE, ..., BlendMesh 2, light 1.0) -- mesh 2, bsh02, drawn again with its own index as the BlendMesh, so added and unlit at full light. Here it is drawn as that glow alone.",
  "sounds_from": "ZzzOpenData.cpp:3793-3797: mMagicSkull loaded twice, SetMonsterSound(..., 186, -1, -1, -1, 187) -- offsets from SOUND_MONSTER_BULL1 = 210: 396 MAGICSKULL1 to walk, 397 MAGICSKULL2 (the same file) to die, no attack sound (DSPlaySound.h:337-338). Wired as magicskeleton_* in sounds.json.",
  "islands_from": "40 islands for 804 triangles. Island 0 (56, u 0.45-0.72) is the .obj's whole bons group, the skull -- bone; 12-39, two triangles each over the whole sheet, are bsh03's 28 wisp quads; the rest bsh01's robe and plate and bsh02's strip. All but the skull cloth. They arrived as skin, the monster profile's default.",
